# hsv

- Label: HSV Adjust
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 5
- Parameters: 14 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/hsv.html
- Summary (EN): Converts images between RGB and HSV so HSV values can be edited and converted back; also applies global hue, saturation and value adjustments. The page is titled HSV Adjust.
- Résumé (FR) : Convertit entre RGB et HSV pour modifier la teinte, la saturation et la luminosité, puis reconvertit le résultat en RGB.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the layer, VDB or attribute to process", "hueshift: optional per-pixel hue amount", "saturation: optional per-pixel saturation amount", "value: optional per-pixel brightness amount", "mask: optional per-pixel mask amount"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Operation", "meaning": "Hue/Sat/Val Adjust, Convert RGB to HSV, or Convert HSV to RGB"}, {"name": "Hue Shift", "meaning": "rotates hues by a number of degrees; grays are unaffected"}, {"name": "Hue Shift Mode", "meaning": "Min/Max remaps the hueshift input to degrees; Width remaps it to a degree range"}, {"name": "Saturation Scale / Saturation Shift", "meaning": "multiply or add to saturation"}, {"name": "Value Scale / Value Shift", "meaning": "multiply or add to brightness"}, {"name": "Keep Luminance", "meaning": "preserves perceived brightness when hues change"}, {"name": "Mask", "meaning": "blends the new result with the original; default 1 uses only the new value"}]

- Caveats: ["Saturation Shift is mainly for reducing saturation; increasing it can give grayscale areas random colors.", "Enable Treat RGBA as Premultiplied if alpha is premultiplied."]

